---
import ResourcePage from "../components/ResourcePage.astro";
import { resourceByPath } from "../config/resources";
import { primarySources } from "../config/site";

const resource = resourceByPath["/24-7-rn-coverage"];
const contents = [
  { href: "#requirement", label: "Monthly reporting requirement" },
  { href: "#what-to-report", label: "What to report" },
  { href: "#coverage-v-minutes", label: "Coverage versus RN minutes" },
  { href: "#evidence", label: "Records to retain" },
  { href: "#workflow", label: "A practical monthly workflow" },
  { href: "#caremin-role", label: "How CareMin supports monitoring" },
  { href: "#sources", label: "Primary sources" },
];
const sources = [
  {
    title: "24/7 registered nurse reporting",
    url: primarySources.rnReporting,
    note: "Monthly reporting scope, absence information and due date",
  },
  {
    title: "24/7 registered nurse requirement",
    url: "https://www.health.gov.au/our-work/care-minutes-registered-nurses-aged-care/24-7-rns",
    note: "Requirement, exemptions and provider responsibilities",
  },
  {
    title: "Care Minutes Performance Statement",
    url: primarySources.performanceStatement,
    note: "Annual statement requirement for monthly RN coverage percentages",
  },
  {
    title: "Aged Care Rules 2025",
    url: primarySources.agedCareRules,
    note: "Current legislative text",
  },
];
---

<ResourcePage
  resource={resource}
  eyebrow="Reporting guide"
  intro="Registered residential aged care providers report RN coverage for every approved home each calendar month. A reliable process must identify coverage gaps, preserve the underlying timeline, and keep coverage separate from the calculation of RN care minutes."
  contents={contents}
  sources={sources}
  relatedPaths={[
    "/care-minutes-performance-statement",
    "/qfr-care-minutes-reporting",
    "/care-minutes-audit-preparation",
  ]}
>
  <section id="requirement" class="resource-section" aria-labelledby="requirement-title">
    <div class="resource-section-heading">
      <p class="resource-section-number">01</p>
      <h2 id="requirement-title">The monthly reporting requirement</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="key-facts" aria-label="RN reporting key facts">
      <div>
        <span>Reporting cycle</span><strong>Every calendar month</strong><p>
          Report separately for each approved residential care home.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Due</span><strong>7th day of the next month</strong><p>
          By 11:59 pm AEST under current department guidance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Submission</span><strong>GPMS</strong><p>
          Manual entry and business-to-government submission options are available.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      Every registered provider must report, including a provider whose home has an exemption from
      the 24/7 RN requirement. The reporting obligation is therefore broader than simply recording
      whether a home believes it met the requirement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-to-report" class="resource-section" aria-labelledby="what-to-report-title">
    <div class="resource-section-heading">
      <p class="resource-section-number">02</p>
      <h2 id="what-to-report-title">What to report when an RN was not onsite and on duty</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Current department guidance requires each period of 30 minutes or more without an RN onsite
      and on duty to be reported. Periods shorter than 30 minutes are not reported as a gap.
    </p>
    <div
      class="responsive-table"
      tabindex="0"
      role="region"
      aria-label="RN absence reporting fields"
    >
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Start and end of each absence</th><td
              >Establishes the duration and affected calendar day.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Planned or unplanned</th><td
              >Explains whether the gap was anticipated.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Delegated nursing responsibility</th><td
              >Records who held responsibility while an RN was absent.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">On-call support and clinical-record access</th><td
              >Documents support available during the absence.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Resident transfer option</th><td
              >Required information when the home had one or more reportable absences.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Recruitment processes</th><td
              >Required information when the home had one or more reportable absences.</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="regulatory-note">
      <strong>Use the government reporting channel.</strong>
      <p>
        The department’s Excel RN coverage tool can help providers calculate coverage, but the
        department states that it is not an approved reporting form and is not mandatory.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="coverage-v-minutes"
    class="resource-section"
    aria-labelledby="coverage-v-minutes-title"
  >
    <div class="resource-section-heading">
      <p class="resource-section-number">03</p>
      <h2 id="coverage-v-minutes-title">RN coverage is not the same measure as RN care minutes</h2>
    </div>
    <div
      class="comparison-table"
      role="group"
      aria-label="RN coverage and RN care minutes comparison"
    >
      <div class="comparison-head">
        <span>Measure</span><span>24/7 RN coverage</span><span>RN care minutes</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Question answered</strong><p>
          Was an RN onsite and on duty throughout the period?
        </p><p>How many eligible RN worked minutes were delivered per occupied bed day?</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Time basis</strong><p>Continuous clock coverage</p><p>
          Eligible worked hours divided by occupied bed days
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Primary reporting</strong><p>Monthly RN coverage report</p><p>
          Quarterly labour-hours and care-minute reporting
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Common risk</strong><p>Small gaps hidden by a monthly percentage</p><p>
          Ineligible or non-worked hours included in the numerator
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      A home can meet an RN care-minute target and still have a reportable coverage gap. It can also
      maintain continuous RN coverage while falling short of its RN care-minute target. Both views
      need their own source records and review controls.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="evidence" class="resource-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <div class="resource-section-heading">
      <p class="resource-section-number">04</p>
      <h2 id="evidence-title">Records to retain behind the monthly percentage</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="audit-checklist">
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span><div>
          <strong>Planned RN roster</strong><p>
            The expected coverage by date, start time, end time, and person.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span><div>
          <strong>Actual attendance</strong><p>
            Worked-time, leave, replacement, call-out, and agency records used to establish what
            occurred.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span><div>
          <strong>Coverage-gap register</strong><p>
            Exact gap duration, planned or unplanned status, and affected home.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span><div>
          <strong>Response record</strong><p>
            Delegation, on-call arrangements, access to clinical records, transfers, recruitment,
            and corrective action.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span><div>
          <strong>Review and submission record</strong><p>
            Calculation method, reviewer, approval, submitted value, submission date, and later
            corrections.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="workflow" class="resource-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="resource-section-heading">
      <p class="resource-section-number">05</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-title">A practical monthly workflow</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="process-ledger" aria-label="Monthly RN coverage workflow">
      <li>
        <span>01</span><strong>Bring planned and actual records together</strong><p>
          Use the latest roster, attendance, leave, agency, and replacement information.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>02</span><strong>Construct the coverage timeline</strong><p>
          Resolve overlaps, missing end times, cross-midnight shifts, and duplicated records.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>03</span><strong>Investigate every break in continuity</strong><p>
          Confirm whether the apparent break is a real absence or a data-quality issue.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>04</span><strong>Document reportable absences</strong><p>
          Record each gap of 30 minutes or more and the required contextual information.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>05</span><strong>Review, approve, and submit</strong><p>
          Retain the reviewed calculation and use GPMS or the available business-to-government
          channel.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="caremin-role" class="resource-section" aria-labelledby="caremin-role-title">
    <div class="resource-section-heading">
      <p class="resource-section-number">06</p>
      <h2 id="caremin-role-title">How CareMin supports RN coverage monitoring</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      CareMin presents a daily coverage timeline and monthly summary alongside care-minute
      performance. Teams can investigate apparent gaps using the underlying source record, keep the
      coverage calculation separate from care-minute calculations, and export a reviewable summary.
    </p>
    <p>
      CareMin supports preparation and monitoring; providers still submit required RN information
      through the government reporting channel.
    </p>
  </section>
</ResourcePage>
